#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# centered_interval

#% text
# `centered_interval(c, r)` represents the interval of the numbers within `r` of `c`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Functions give f(c) with the radius r times the largest |f'| at c - r, c and c + r (an estimate, not a rigorous enclosure; balls give those).

#% item
# `centered_interval([[m, e, rm, re], p])` reads the centre m 2^e and the radius rm 2^re.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
centered_interval(2, 0.1)
#% output
#= centered_interval(2, 0.1)

#% cell
airy_ai(centered_interval(2, 0.1))
#% output
#= centered_interval(0.03527351107369801, 0.0053209089578315555)

#% cell
centered_interval(1, 1/10) + 2
#% output
#= centered_interval(3.0, 0.1000000000000055)

